        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0453" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/519.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Attorney General to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The United States attorney of the western district of Texas has wired that Madero
                    may now appear in his district at any hour, and that he does not deem evidence
                    at hand against him sufficient to meet technical requirements necessary to
                    constitute violation of neutrality laws. Before replying I would appreciate a
                    full statement from Mexican embassy as to the evidence for the use of the United
                    States attorney.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wickersham</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
